### Generate Images with AI SDK and Google Gemini 2.5 Flash

Source: https://ai-sdk.dev/cookbook/guides/google-gemini-image-generation

Use the `generateText` function with the `google/gemini-2.5-flash-image` model to create images from a text prompt. Generated images are returned as `Uint8Array` data in `result.files`.

```javascript
import { generateText } from 'ai';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import 'dotenv/config';


async function generateImage() {
  const result = await generateText({
    model: 'google/gemini-2.5-flash-image',
    prompt:
      'Create a picture of a nano banana dish in a fancy restaurant with a Gemini theme',
  });


  // Save generated images
  for (const file of result.files) {
    if (file.mediaType.startsWith('image/')) {
      const timestamp = Date.now();
      const fileName = `generated-${timestamp}.png`;


      fs.mkdirSync('output', { recursive: true });
      await fs.promises.writeFile(`output/${fileName}`, file.uint8Array);


      console.log(`Generated and saved image: output/${fileName}`);
    }
  }
}

generateImage().catch(console.error);
```

--------------------------------

### Generate images using Google Gemini Interactions

Source: https://ai-sdk.dev/providers/ai-sdk-providers/google

Use the responseFormat option with `{ type: 'image' }` to generate images directly from Gemini image-capable models without tool wrapping.

```typescript
import {
  google,
  type GoogleLanguageModelInteractionsOptions,
} from '@ai-sdk/google';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const result = await generateText({ 
  model: google.interactions('gemini-3-pro-image-preview'),
  prompt: 'Generate an image of a comic cat in a spaceship.',
  providerOptions: {
    google: {
      responseFormat: [{ type: 'image' }],
    } satisfies GoogleLanguageModelInteractionsOptions,
  },
});

for (const file of result.files) {
  if (file.mediaType.startsWith('image/')) {
    // file.uint8Array | file.base64 | file.mediaType
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Send a base64-encoded image string in a user message (TypeScript)

Source: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/foundations/prompts

Convert a local image file to a base64 string using `toString('base64')` and include it in a user message. This is an alternative for embedding image data.

```ts
const result = await generateText({
  model: __MODEL__,
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        { type: 'text', text: 'Describe the image in detail.' },
        {
          type: 'file',
          mediaType: 'image',
          data: fs.readFileSync('./data/comic-cat.png').toString('base64'),
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
```

--------------------------------

### Generate Images using Multi-modal Language Models

Source: https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-core/image-generation

Access generated images from multi-modal language models like Gemini by reading from the files property of the response.

```typescript
import { google } from '@ai-sdk/google';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const result = await generateText({
  model: google('gemini-2.5-flash-image'),
  prompt: 'Generate an image of a comic cat',
});

for (const file of result.files) {
  if (file.mediaType.startsWith('image/')) {
    // The file object provides multiple data formats:
    // Access images as base64 string, Uint8Array binary data, or check type
    // - file.base64: string (data URL format)
    // - file.uint8Array: Uint8Array (binary data)
    // - file.mediaType: string (e.g. "image/png")
  }
}
```

### Generate and Edit Images with Google Gemini 2.5 Flash > Generating Images

Source: https://ai-sdk.dev/resources/recipes/guides/google-gemini-image-generation

Because Gemini 2.5 Flash Image is a language model with multimodal capabilities, you use the generateText or streamText functions instead of generateImage to create images. The model determines which modality to respond in based on your prompt and configuration. Generated images are returned as Uint8Array data in the result.files array.

